  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Central Liberia Rice and Vegetable Value Chain Proposal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the end of Liberia&#x2019;s violent civil war in 2003, the government of Liberia (GoL) has adopted policy reforms and taken steps toward securing economic growth and rebuilding institutions and infrastructure.  However, Liberia remains one of the world&#x2019;s poorest countries with a GDP per capita of $362 and a ranking of 169 on the 2009 Human Development Index. The food security situation in Liberia is a chronic one rooted in pervasive poverty with lots of constraints, i.e physical, human and capital.</narrative>
  </description>
